From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orangepi6 kernel-7 port
Subject: [PATCH] cix adapt Sky1 drivers to 7.x kernel APIs

Build fixes for kernel 7.x API changes in Sky1 drivers that merged cleanly
but no longer compile:
- armchina-npu: pm_runtime_put() returns void
- xhci-plat (Sky1 ACPI LPM detection): HCS_U1/U2_LATENCY are now masks
- linlon VPU: strncpy() replaced by strscpy()
- CIX display drivers: struct drm_atomic_state renamed to drm_atomic_commit,
  DRM_COLOR_FORMAT_* bit masks replaced by BIT(DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_*).
  This is partial: linlon-dp and trilin still need the new private-object
  (atomic_create_state) and panel allocation APIs, so DRM_CIX is disabled
  on this track (kernel.conf KCONFIG_EXTRA).
---
